 It depends on your database, so I will be precise.
- PostgreSQL: ALTER TABLE my_table ALTER COLUMN my_column TYPE INTEGER USING my_column::INTEGER;
- MySQL: ALTER TABLE my_table MODIFY COLUMN my_column INT;
- SQL Server: ALTER TABLE my_table ALTER COLUMN my_column INT;
- pandas: df['my_column'] = df['my_column'].astype(int)
Back up the data first, because a careless conversion can truncate or fail on values that do not fit.
